hey what's up guys it's rob and welcome  to my tutorial for the easy minute  wallet  today i'm going to show you a quick and  easy way that you can store your cash  and cards if you don't want to carry  around a big bulky wallet like this  it's a cool origami model that's a  modified design by humiaki huzida and it  has  four spots with two inside pockets and  two  outside sleeves that you can store your  cash and cards it's a really thin  sleek design that's simple to make and a  lot of fun to fold  i'm also announcing the launch of my  brand new patreon page  i've always wanted to interact with my  subscribers so now available  on my rob's world patreon page are three  separate tiers that you can join where  you can get shout outs on my channel  join live sessions and discord chats or  get one-on-one  extra help sessions you can sign up now  to join a community and show your  support and get the inside scoop also on  new ideas like this duct tape hat that i  made  i might even use your ideas for new  videos on my channel i'll post a link in  the video and also the description so be  sure to check it out  to make the wallet we'll need a letter  size or a4 paper of any color  and you can also use cardstock if you  want the wallet to be extra sturdy  once you have the paper let's jump right  into it hold the paper with the longer  edges up and down and take the top and  fold  it down to the bottom line up the edges  and make a nice sharp crease  on top then you can unfold the paper  and we're going to take the top and  bottom edges folding it into that new  crease that we made  fold the top down and make a crease and  then fold the bottom edge  directly next to the top edge in the  middle and make a crease on the bottom  once again unfold the edges we're going  to take the top edge and fold it down  about half of an inch or the width of  your pinky  take a small portion of the top and just  fold it inwards like this  and make a nice sharp crease on top so  that it looks like this  do the same on the bottom folding it  about half of an inch  once you've done that make a nice sharp  crease on the bottom  now we can take the two top corners and  fold them inwards to this first line  right here  airplane fold it in like this and make a  nice sharp crease on the top  so that it looks like that do the same  on the top left  folding the top corner inwards and  creasing now we could flip it around and  do the same on the other side  airplane fold the two top corners  inwards and  make a nice sharp crease on top now we  can take the top and bottom and fold  them  on this crease right here fold it and  flatten it and then fold the top edge in  and flatten it as well once it's nice  and flat i'm going to turn it to the  left like this  and pick it up you'll see these two  corners here i'm going to press on them  and fold the top edge down along the  corners or a little below them  once it's folded down just make a nice  sharp crease and reinforce it with your  fingernail like this  then you can unfold the edge and do the  same on the other side  press on the corners fold the edge down  and give it a nice sharp crease  then you can unfold the edge and we're  going to fold backwards  on that crease that we just made once we  fold it backwards then we could  flatten it out and press on it now we  could flip the whole thing  upside down and fold backwards on the  top edge here  just like we did on the other side then  you could take the bottom edge and  you'll see  we're going to tuck it underneath this  little triangular pocket  slide it underneath the pocket and do  the same on the other side  just like this so it's underneath now we  could flatten everything out  and we can once again pick it up take  the left edge and fold it across  on this vertical line and make sure it's  nice and flat once again  now we've completed the minute wallet  and you could take the card and slip it  into the left side pocket  take the cash and slip it into the right  just lift the pocket  open like this and tuck it in and you  also have two additional sleeves on the  outside that you can also use  for cards or cash thank you guys so much  for watching my tutorial for the easy  minute wallet i hope you guys enjoyed it  if you did be sure to give it a thumbs  up down below  and also don't forget to subscribe and  click that notification bell  also be sure to check out my patreon  page and let me know down in the  comments below if you want to see  the duct tape hat or whatever you'd like  to see leave a comment on here  i'd love to start a new community on my  patreon page and connect with you guys  and do live sessions i think it would be  a lot of fun  i got a lot of new ideas coming up so if  you're not subscribed be sure to click  that notification bell and i'll see you  guys soon
 

